 "result_text": "I changed the Data Format 3 check in `ruuvitag_sensor/ruuvi.py` so it accepts the shorter payloads that RuuviFW 1.2.8 sends. I haven't run the tests or tried it against real tag data.\n\nBefore, `_get_data_format_3` rejected any payload that wasn't exactly 54 hex characters. Firmware 1.2.8 trims trailing NULLs, so valid Format 3 data failed that length check. It now accepts anything from 18 to 54 characters. It still requires `03` at the format position, and it pads the payload with zeros back to 54 characters before returning it, so the decoder gets the full-length data it expects.\n\nI didn't touch the Format 2/4 detection, since it searches the decoded text for `ruu.vi/#` or `r/` and doesn't depend on length. I also didn't do #29, which the issue mentioned.",
